kind=task
title=Add rate limiting to the public API
source=cursor.agent
project=api-gateway
---
[goal]
Add per-token rate limiting to the public API so a single client cannot
exhaust the shared worker pool.

[context]
The gateway lives in src/gateway/server.py and routes through
src/gateway/middleware.py. There is no rate limiter today. We saw one client
send 12k req/min last week and starve everyone else. A Redis instance is
already available at config/redis.yaml.

[constraints]
- No breaking changes to the existing response schema
- Limits must be configurable per API token, not global
- Add a regression test before merging
- Do not add new third-party dependencies beyond redis-py

[handoff]
- to=any   do=implement a sliding-window limiter in src/gateway/middleware.py
- to=any   do=load per-token limits from config/limits.yaml
- to=any   do=add a test in tests/test_rate_limit.py that fails on main
- to=human do=review the diff and approve the limit defaults
- [x] reproduced the starvation with a load test on main@a1b2c3d
END CRUMB
